SUMMARY:Three-day panigiri of Kato Garouna
LOCATION:Kato Garouna\, Corfu\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kato Garouna\, above Agios Gordios on the west coast\, is famous on Corfu for its musicians ('Ta paidia ap' to Garouna') and throws a three-day panigiri from 16 August with its own players\, long tables of pastitsada and sofrito and dancing every night\; the village also does a wine festival on a Saturday at the very end of August. Twenty minutes from town\; go on the first night\, which is the most local.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#kato-garouna-three-day-panigiri-of-kato-garouna
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#kato-garouna-three-day-panigiri-of-kato-garouna
